{
  "$comment": [
    "Proposed ar patterns for src/data/claims-lint.json (patterns.ar of each rule) and src/data/keyword-map.json (seOwned.ar additions, seOwnedLead.ar, reserved.G1.ar). Drafted with the ar copy (M3, T3); merge is the lead's decision (wave-2 note).",
    "Covers every claims-lint rule with per-locale patterns except selection-translate and jargon (they already have ar) and the '*'-only rules io-home and engine-claim.",
    "Written for the Unicode-aware lint data of bb689eb: \\w is a letter, mark or digit of any script (so ترجم\\w* also covers ترجمتها and ترجمةً with tanwin), \\b / \\W work at Arabic word edges. Arabic attaches و ف ب ل ك and the article ال to the next word, so most patterns are substrings with an optional (ال)? rather than whole words; \\p{M}* stands where a shadda or haraka may sit inside a stem (تعلّم, يتعرّف); [إا] / [أا] accept a missing hamza. \\s also matches the copy's no-break spaces (U+00A0).",
    "Tested in a private copy: 0 hits on src/locales/ar.json (exempt keys as in claims-lint.json), every rule hits its counter-examples (docs/redesign-2026/ops/m3/ar-qa.md, appendix A), and the generic learning phrases of doc 03 §1.4 (لمتعلمي اللغات …) pass seOwned."
  ],
